ffpfsc-pkg-tool bundles the following third-party components:

  LibProsperoPkg 1.2.0 (net9.0)                 — GPL-3.0-or-later
      Copyright (C) 2026 SvenGDK; the 1.2.0 line is drakmor's fork
      (https://github.com/drakmor/LibProsperoPkg, commit 8551d2f "Version
      1.2.0"; upstream https://github.com/SvenGDK/LibProsperoPKG, tag v1.2).
      The assembly was taken compiled from the author's a53-fpkg 0.5 release.
      THE BUNDLED COPY IS MODIFIED (2026-09-25): two IL patches applied with
      the patcher in src/ffpfsc-pkg-tool/patches/CecilPatch — drm_type=16 for
      Application volumes, and FilterFakeLibraryDirectory made a no-op. What
      and why: src/ffpfsc-pkg-tool/patches/README.md. Pristine and patched
      assemblies with SHA-256 sums: src/ffpfsc-pkg-tool/lib/.

  BCnEncoder.NET 2.3.0                          — MIT OR Unlicense (NuGet)
  CommunityToolkit.HighPerformance 8.4.0        — MIT (NuGet)
  Magick.NET-Q8-AnyCPU + Magick.NET.Core 14.15.0 — Apache-2.0 (NuGet); the
      embedded native ImageMagick library is under the ImageMagick License
  .NET 9 runtime (self-contained)               — MIT

Because the packaged runtime includes GPL-3-licensed code (LibProsperoPkg),
ffpfsc-pkg-tool as distributed is a GPL-3-or-later work. The rest of
ps5-ffpfsc-ultra is unchanged; the GPL scope covers this native binary only.
The wrapper's own source lives in backend/native/src/ffpfsc-pkg-tool/.
